-- ================================================================
-- StreetRise — Migration 045: Miami-Dade Transit static GTFS
--
-- NOT APPLIED. Runbook: docs/apply-migrations-042-046.md.
-- Requires migration 042 (the tables).
--
-- 6,973 stops, 122 routes from Miami-Dade Transit's published bundle —
-- by far the largest of the four feeds, and the one covering StreetRise's
-- densest listing set outside Tampa. Generated by
-- `scripts/build-transit-sql.ts`; DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
--
-- ── No feed_info.txt, so two fields are derived ─────────────
-- Miami-Dade omits `feed_info.txt` entirely, which GTFS permits. Both fields
-- it would have supplied are load-bearing, so both fall back:
--
--   • `feed_valid_until` ← the latest end_date among active calendar rows,
--     giving 2027-12-31. This is what makes the app STOP asserting a network
--     it can no longer vouch for, so it cannot be left NULL.
--   • `feed_version` ← 'derived-add7dd65cc6b', a SHA-1 over the files that
--     describe the network (routes, stops, calendars) but NOT stop_times.
--     A timetable tweak that moves departures without adding or removing a
--     stop should update rows in place, which ON CONFLICT already does; what
--     the version has to detect is a stop LEAVING the network, because the
--     trailing DELETE uses it to retire those. A NULL version would make that
--     DELETE a permanent no-op and stops would accumulate forever.
--
-- The derived version changes if and only if the network does, so a re-run
-- against an unchanged feed is a true no-op.
--
-- ── What it corrects, and what it confirms ──────────────────
-- Measured against the 25 Miami-Dade listings live today: 5 currently say
-- public_transit_accessible = FALSE while sitting within 400 m of a stop and
-- will be raised — Caring for Miami (71 m), Americans for Immigrant Justice
-- (72 m), Branches South Dade (141 m), Miami Bridge Homestead (320 m) and
-- Chapman Partnership Homestead (355 m).
--
-- Just as usefully, it CONFIRMS the hand-set flags from migration 032: 18 of
-- the 19 already-TRUE rows are inside 400 m, most of them within 100. The one
-- exception, Branches North Dade, measures 400.4 m — over the line by a
-- rounding error, and left alone, because this migration never lowers a flag.
-- That is a good result for hand-entered data and worth recording.
--
-- No fare files ship with this feed, so every route lands fare_price NULL /
-- is_fare_free FALSE — unknown, not free.
-- ================================================================


